## Protocol discovery (original to this repository)

The following findings were derived in this project and are not from emokit:

  * the dongle serial encodes its manufacture date (`UD` + `YYYYMMDD` + counter)
  * `UD2017`+ serials fall through emokit's literal `startswith("UD2016")` test
  * the 2016+ payload is **16-bit little-endian** fields at byte offsets
    2,4,…,30 — emokit used big-endian
  * the payload is **32 bytes**, not the 64 the "new format" code assumes
  * fields must be read as **unsigned** counts; a signed view manufactures
    65535-count artefacts when the high byte crosses 0x7F/0x80

See `eeg-vault/02-software/ud2016-crypto-crack.md`.
